# {{lb|en|derogatory|informal}} A [[hidden#Adjective|hidden]] [[enemy#Noun|enemy]].
#: {{synonyms|en|backstabber}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1906|author=w:Horatio Alger|title=Randy of the River|chapter=6|passage=I trusted him too much from the start. He has proved to be a '''snake in the grass'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1914|author=w:William MacLeod Raine|title=A Daughter of the Dons|chapter=5|passage=Is he not here to throw us out—a thief, a spy, a '''snake in the grass'''?}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1973|author=w:Charlie Daniels|title=w:Uneasy Rider|passage=He's a '''snake in the grass''', I tell you guys<br>He may look dumb but that's just a disguise<br>He's a mastermind in the ways of espionage.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Nov 21 2008|author=Bruce Crumley|title=Which Woman Will Lead France's Socialists?|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120116083204/http://www.time.com/time/world/article/0,8599,1861119,00.html|journal=Time|passage=Following her presidential defeat, Royal stunned many observers by publicly dumping Socialist Party leader François Hollande — her companion and the father of her four children — and announcing she'd seek his post during the current election. To some, that made Royal the symbol of the strong, modern woman in politics; to others, it cast her as the classic '''snake in the grass'''.}}

